ld Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134411374,imgsize-199332.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Iran ready reopen Hormuz within 7 days, negotiate if the US lifts blockade]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134411572.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-ready-reopen-hormuz-within-7-days-negotiate-if-the-us-lifts-blockade/articleshow/134411572.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-ready-reopen-hormuz-within-7-days-negotiate-if-the-us-lifts-blockade/articleshow/134411572.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T17:31:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134411872,imgsize-156540.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Detroit lawyer bought Berry Gordy's Motown mansion for $250K in 2002, sold it for $1.65M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134409569.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A century-old Detroit mansion with deep ties to the city’s music and industrial history once changed hands for just $250,000 before a painstaking restoration helped it sell for $1.65 million. Known as the Motown Mansion, the 10,500-square-foot residence at 918 W. Boston Blvd. was built in 1916-17 for lumberman Nels Michelson and later became the home of Motown Records founder Berry Gordy Jr. Historic Detroit identifies the property as the Nels Michelson Mansion and documents its origins, architecture and notable owners. Gordy bought the house in 1967 and lived there during a pivotal period for Motown before eventually selling it to Detroit attorney Cynthia F. Reaves, who restored the landmark and later sold it in 2017.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2002-a-detroit-lawyer-bought-berry-gordys-1917-motown-mansion-for-250000-restored-the-10500-sq-ft-landmark-and-sold-it-for-1-65-million-in-2017/articleshow/134409569.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2002-a-detroit-lawyer-bought-berry-gordys-1917-motown-mansion-for-250000-restored-the-10500-sq-ft-landmark-and-sold-it-for-1-65-million-in-2017/articleshow/134409569.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134409726,imgsize-1877332.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[17 years after losing his arm, he can feel again with a bionic limb]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134410160.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/a-florida-man-lost-his-left-arm-after-a-35-foot-fall-at-16-17-years-later-he-is-the-first-to-take-home-a-thought-controlled-bionic-arm-that-can-restore-his-sense-of-touch/articleshow/134410160.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/a-florida-man-lost-his-left-arm-after-a-35-foot-fall-at-16-17-years-later-he-is-the-first-to-take-home-a-thought-controlled-bionic-arm-that-can-restore-his-sense-of-touch/articleshow/134410160.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T16:38:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134410397,imgsize-371587.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Wyoming shed was a 140-year-old Chinese laundry; it will become a museum exhibit after restoration]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134407889.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A weathered Wyoming cabin used as a storage shed for decades turned out to be a 140-year-old Chinese laundry and bathhouse owned by Sam Sing. After an eight-year effort, the historic building has been moved to a museum, where it will be restored and used to tell the story of Lander’s early Chinese community.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-weathered-wyoming-cabin-used-as-a-storage-shed-turned-out-to-be-a-140-year-old-chinese-laundry-after-an-eight-year-rescue-effort-the-building-has-been-moved-to-a-museum-for-restoration/articleshow/134407889.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-weathered-wyoming-cabin-used-as-a-storage-shed-turned-out-to-be-a-140-year-old-chinese-laundry-after-an-eight-year-rescue-effort-the-building-has-been-moved-to-a-museum-for-restoration/articleshow/134407889.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134408271,imgsize-255042.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Elvis superfan buys $150K Graceland-inspired home, plans to rent out backyard caravans]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134406497.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Elvis Presley superfan Claire Starring has bought “Lil’ Graceland”, a Memphis home inspired by the singer’s famous estate, for $150,000. The three-bedroom property was previously bought for $55,000 in 2017. Starring plans to keep its retro interiors, remodel two backyard caravans for guests and continue using the property as a short-term rental, recording studio and film and photo location.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/an-elvis-superfan-paid-150000-for-a-memphis-home-inspired-by-graceland-which-its-previous-owners-bought-for-55000-she-now-plans-to-turn-its-backyard-caravans-into-another-source-of-income/articleshow/134406497.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/an-elvis-superfan-paid-150000-for-a-memphis-home-inspired-by-graceland-which-its-previous-owners-bought-for-55000-she-now-plans-to-turn-its-backyard-caravans-into-another-source-of-income/articleshow/134406497.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134407767,imgsize-256300.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1951 Mickey Mantle photo used for 1952 Topps card sells privately for record $3 million in 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134407404.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An astonishing 1951 photograph of Mickey Mantle has shattered records, fetching $3 million at auction. This particular image laid the groundwork for his legendary 1952 Topps baseball card. Captured just before Mantle stepped onto the field for the New York Yankees, the rare PSA Type I image has found a new home with collector Ron Firman, marking a historic peak for Type I sports photographs.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-1951-mickey-mantle-photograph-used-to-create-his-famous-1952-topps-card-has-sold-privately-for-3-million-more-than-tripling-the-previous-record-for-an-unsigned-sports-photograph/articleshow/134407404.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-1951-mickey-mantle-photograph-used-to-create-his-famous-1952-topps-card-has-sold-privately-for-3-million-more-than-tripling-the-previous-record-for-an-unsigned-sports-photograph/articleshow/134407404.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134407557,imgsize-1736316.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Las Vegas has a hidden world where hundreds live in 600 miles of flood tunnels]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134407773.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/las-vegas-has-a-hidden-world-beneath-its-streets-where-hundreds-of-people-live-inside-600-miles-of-flood-tunnels/articleshow/134407773.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/las-vegas-has-a-hidden-world-beneath-its-streets-where-hundreds-of-people-live-inside-600-miles-of-flood-tunnels/articleshow/134407773.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T14:40:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134407773,imgsize-63193.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US couple donates $250 million to animal support and welfare organisations for access to pet healthcare]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134408612.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-couple-donates-250-million-to-animal-support-and-welfare-organisations-allowing-veterinary-care-access-to-millions-of-families-and-their-pets-over-the-next-five-years/articleshow/134408612.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-couple-donates-250-million-to-animal-support-and-welfare-organisations-al